{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792127799,"nonce":"dMgQGnMb13RSCHuknAduobnCi7E=","message":"Decision (user 2026-10-15): a live link whose final URL is a USAJOBS posting (www.usajobs.gov job announcement) counts as settled, as a special case of the board-copy rule. Reason: USAJOBS is the federal apply entry point; its Apply button checks the signed-in USAJOBS profile and then hands off to the agency system (usually USA Staffing), which cannot be reached without signing in, so retries can never find a better link. Note the reason in code and in spec 015.","files":null}]}